{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.AlgebraMap","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.End"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.mixing_not_in_letter_algebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.mixing_not_in_letter_algebra","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L157-L166","doc":"**A mixing coupling is not in the single-letter algebra.**  For any\n`OrbitalMixingSpec` over `σ`, the coupling `X` is not `p(σ)` for any polynomial\n`p`.  In particular it is not in the image of the two-strand Hecke algebra\ngenerated by `σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.mixes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.mixes","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L155-L155","doc":"The coupling has a nonzero D-wave matrix element out of the S-wave. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.X","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L153-L153","doc":"The coupling operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.piD_vS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.piD_vS","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L151-L151","doc":"The S-wave vector has no D-wave component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.piD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.piD","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L149-L149","doc":"The functional reading the D-wave (`ℓ = 2`) component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.eigen","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L147-L147","doc":"`vS` is an eigenvector of the letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.c","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L145-L145","doc":"Its eigenvalue under the interface letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.vS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.vS","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L143-L143","doc":"The S-wave (`ℓ = 0`) vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec.mk","kind":"ctor","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L141-L141","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.OrbitalMixingSpec","kind":"structure","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L129-L155","doc":"**Specification of an orbital-mixing carrier** on a module `M` with an\ninterface letter `σ`.\n\n* `vS` — the `ℓ = 0` vector, an eigenvector of the letter (eigenvalue `c`);\n* `piD` — a linear functional reading the `ℓ = 2` component, which vanishes on\n  `vS` (the S-wave vector has no D-wave component);\n* `X` — the coupling, with a nonzero D-wave component of `X vS`.\n\nThis is a requirements structure, **not** a conjecture: abstract instances\nexist in any module with two independent vectors.  The open question\n(`qou-7zob`) is an instance whose `X` is derived from braid data; that is not\nencoded here and no instance is provided. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.wigner_lock_same_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.wigner_lock_same_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L114-L127","doc":"**Wigner lock.**  Let `PS`, `PI` be the spin and isospin exchanges and\n`PS * PI` the combined exchange.  A `³S₁` vector (`PS = +1`, `PI = -1`) and a\n`¹S₀` vector (`PS = -1`, `PI = +1`) are both `-1` eigenvectors of the combined\nexchange, so every polynomial in it acts on both by `p(-1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.exchange_even_same_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.exchange_even_same_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L100-L112","doc":"**Exchange sees only `ℓ mod 2`.**  If the exchange `E` acts on a vector\n`vS` of sector `ℓ` and a vector `vD` of sector `ℓ + 2` by the inversion signs\n`(-1)^ℓ` and `(-1)^(ℓ+2)`, then every polynomial in `E` acts on both by the\nsame scalar `p((-1)^ℓ)`.  For `ℓ = 0`: no element of the algebra generated by\nthe exchange distinguishes an S-wave vector from a D-wave vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.exchange_sign_period_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.exchange_sign_period_two","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L93-L98","doc":"**Exchange parity of the orbital sector.**  The relative-coordinate\nexchange acts on sector `ℓ` by `(-1)^ℓ`; sectors `ℓ` and `ℓ + 2` carry the same\nsign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.aeval_mem_of_eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.aeval_mem_of_eigen","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L85-L91","doc":"**No transfer out of a submodule.**  If `v ∈ N` is an eigenvector of `σ`,\nevery polynomial in `σ` maps `v` back into `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.aeval_apply_of_eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.OrbitalIndexCarrier.aeval_apply_of_eigen","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/OrbitalIndexCarrier.lean#L66-L83","doc":"**Eigenvector transport.**  If `σ v = c • v` then `p(σ) v = p(c) • v` for\nevery polynomial `p`.  No nonzero or field hypothesis is needed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}